    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d36">

                <pb facs="0064" n="46" sameAs="frus:frus1946v02/pg46"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.00119 Council/4–846</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Soviet Foreign Minister</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Molotov</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of
                        State</hi><anchor n="67" xml:id="d36-f1"/></head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Translation]</seg>
                </opener>
                <p>I agree with your proposal to call in Paris on April 25 a meeting of the Council
                    of the Ministers of Foreign Affairs who, in conformity with the understanding at
                    the Moscow Meeting, are connected with the preparation of peace treaties for the
                    forthcoming conference not later than May 1.</p>
                <p>From the Soviet side, instructions have already been sent to London to expedite
                    to the maximum degree the work of the Deputies on the draft peace treaties in
                    order that the questions which remain in disagreement may be considered at the
                    meeting of the Ministers.</p>
                <closer>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-left">
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1946-04-06"><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >April</hi> 6, 1946</date>.</dateline>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d36-f1" n="67" type="source" xml:id="d36-f1-content">
                <p>The original Russian text of this message was transmitted to the Secretary of
                    State on April 8, by the Soviet Ambassador, Nikolai Vasilyevich Novikov.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
